+*   **Limitations:** Structural method requires gradient calculation. Interior culling may remove thin structures if they are fully enclosed. Cylindrical masking is display-specific. Interpolation artifacts may occur near clipped surfaces if classification is not performed before interpolation [S1][S3, S4, S5, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Voxel visibility culling has been developed in various contexts, from scientific visualization of atomic structures to real-time rendering on specialized hardware. The structural visibility metric was introduced in "Visibility-Aware Direct Volume Rendering" [S1]. Geometric clipping methods are common in isosurface extraction pipelines [S2, unofficial]. Interior culling is used in voxel-based game engines and renderers to optimize mesh generation [S3, unofficial]. Cylindrical masking is specific to volumetric display systems like Multivox [S4, unofficial].
+Voxel visibility culling has been developed in various contexts, from scientific visualization of atomic structures to real-time rendering on specialized hardware [S1][S2, S3, S4, S5, S6, unofficial]. The structural visibility metric was introduced in "Visibility-Aware Direct Volume Rendering" [S1]. Geometric clipping methods are implemented in isosurface extraction pipelines to discard instances based on isovalue thresholds [S2, unofficial]. Interior culling is used in voxel-based renderers to optimize mesh generation by removing fully enclosed voxels [S4, unofficial]. Cylindrical masking is specific to volumetric display systems like Multivox [S5, unofficial]. Frustum culling is integrated into GPU-accelerated 3D Gaussian splatting frameworks to rasterize only visible centers [S6, unofficial].
 
